  // One outfield set for all six parks (#730, decision 3) — per-park depth is #713's. These are not
  // the park fence scale: each body keeps its full-size bearing and its fraction of the fence AT
  // THAT BEARING, measured through the circular fence arc on harbor-diamond (AtBatResolver.FenceAt).
  // LF and RF keep 0.7203 of the fence at ∓23.75° (radius 273.13 -> 191.40); CF keeps 0.7625 of it
  // (305 -> 213.50). The two fractions are different, so 110 x 0.70 = 77.00 is the wrong answer.
  "left": {
    "xFt": -77.09,
    "zFt": 175.19
  },
  "center": {
    "xFt": 0,
    "zFt": 213.5
  },
  "right": {
    "xFt": 77.09,
    "zFt": 175.19
  },
  // F2-d (FD-07): the fence the three outfield starts are authored against - the default park's posts. A park that
  // names no outfield start stands each outfielder at his bearing and his fraction of this fence, on its own fence.
